title The option that was TCP reasoning on a UDP socket
prompt fleet baton; the card's PATCHOULI block named three doors out of the port collision, and the third was the cheapest
rota lap 4635, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; it listened for what nobody answered, and the answer was five days old: amphora_udp_reuseaddr_scan.sh has REPORTED these exact seven mantra paths since 20260906 under a reading it deliberately never gates, and no lane had replied
think REDS first: cold pass opened at 084925 and ran the whole lap; pin capacity read pin_deadlocked=1 rows_that_fit=0, so any row this lap booked had to be born on its own shelf
think %700's first repair was the flap counter I built last lap; its second was named as three doors and all three were framed as Keaton's. Door three -- drop SO_REUSEADDR -- turned out to be already SEATED one lane over in amphora/vessel_fetch_delivery.rye under REDS 20260906.154105, with a kernel probe. Adopting a proven repair from a sibling module is mechanical; doors one and two change the wire and stay his
think the option's comment is careful, cites REDS %282, and says why -- and is about TCP. UDP has no TIME_WAIT, so it bought a duplicate bind instead of a rebind
think the census found it in all seven mantra delivery modules, and found 38490/38491 bound by two of them inside ONE tree
obs measured rather than argued: eight concurrent selftests against a build from each side. With the option 12 RecvFailed + 2 Truncated, 0 of 8 green. Without it 13 BindFailed, 1 of 8 green. The green rate was never the claim -- the collision stands, and the kernel names it
obs the read-back matters more than the deletion: deleting a line proves the line is gone, getsockopt proves the socket the kernel handed over carries what the file claims. 7 of 7 read it back
obs the new scan reads git ls-files rather than a find walk, and that choice paid inside the same lap -- amphora's find-walking peer census counts this ship's gitignored .lap/elder_delivery.rye, so the two instruments now read 13 and 12 and the ghost IS the difference. BAKERY closed that same defect in dated_path hours earlier
obs I attempted the index oracle in amphora's scan and WITHDREW it: it fells four legs of that control, whose pens are plain directories rather than repositories, and repairing them is a third frame past the depth-2 bound. Reverted, peer witness re-proven GREEN at 32 behaviors 0 failed, and handed over measured on the card
obs REDS FIRST REORDERED THE LAP MID-ROUND. The roster's cold reading carried stash_record red at records_unlanded=1, and the record was MY OWN lap killed mid-send at 20260911.071505 -- whose log said status GREEN and named every witness, which is that field earning its seating for the second time in one morning
obs that lap had already built DOOR TWO for mantra/recall_tablecloth_query_delivery.rye: both sockets bind port zero, the caller hands its kernel-chosen port to the dependent in argv, the dependent answers one ready byte, and the host reads the caller's address off that datagram. Its own falsifier had fired against a half-fix at 38 of 40 red under four-way concurrency
obs the two repairs COMPOSE rather than compete -- door two removes the collision, door three names what remains. I landed the killed lap's work files unedited via git checkout <stash> -- <paths>, which reads the TREE so the mode survives (the exec-bit rule's own spelling), took none of its card, REDS or index edits, then applied my sweep on top
obs composed reading: mantra_delivery_port_control 0 red of 16 clean against 7 red of 8 for a pen mutant pinned back to 38490; the wire witness GREEN with its concurrency leg
obs four mantra wire-lab witnesses refuse at their device leg -- measured from both sides of this change and with it stashed, identical, so older than this repair and already the welded-witness class %646 books
obs THE INSTRUMENT I BUILT LAST LAP TOOK ITS OWN READING. mantra_query_wire_flap_scan.sh over the repaired guard, 12 repeats: green=12 red=0 flap=no, at loads 14.15 to 18.33. Last lap the same counter over the same guard read 18 green 6 red flap=yes across 24 runs, every red at load 17-19 -- so this reading sits INSIDE that band rather than beside it
obs what that reading does NOT prove: 12 runs with no red is one afternoon's evidence, never a cured race. It is a rate measured under one pier's load, which is testimony and belongs here rather than in a gate
